    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-k/q1-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"(a) The arc length is 6(1.25) = 7.5 cm, [B1] so P = 6 + 6 + 7.5 and the perimeter is 19.5 cm . [M1] [A1] The area is 2(62)(1.25) = 22.5 cm2 . 1 [A1] (b) The equations are r2θ = 45 [M1] and 2r + rθ = 21. [A1] The new area equals 22.5 and its perimeter is 19.5 + 1.5 = 21.\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-k/q1-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"Multiply the perimeter equation by r: 2r2 + r2θ = 21r. Substitute r2θ = 45. Eliminate θ to obtain 2r2 −21r + 45 = (2r −15)(r −3) . [A1] = 0 Then θ = 45/r2 [A1] gives 45/(7.5)2 = 0.8 or 45/32 = 5, yielding (r, θ) = (7.5, 0.8) or (3, 5) . [A1] The second pair describes a major sector: [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 1 is 10 marks.</p>"
    ],
