    "id": "madas/alevel-pure-k/q5",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-k/q5-question-1.svg\" alt=\"( + ) ≡ − cos A B cos A cos B sin A sin B cos ( A − B ) ≡ cos A cos B + sin A sin B a) By using the above identities show that  P + Q   P − Q  cos P − cos Q ≡− 2sin   sin   . ( ) 4  2   2  b) Hence, prove by first principles that d ( cos x ) = − sin x ( ) 6 dx\" style=\"--madas-width:570.7px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-k/q5-question-2.svg\" alt=\"Question diagram\" style=\"--madas-width:576.0px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-k/q5-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"(a) Put A = (P + Q)/2 [B1] [A1] and B = (P −Q)/2. [A1] Indeed P = A + B, Q = A −B; adding gives 2A = P + Q, subtracting gives 2B = P −Q. Expand both cosines: cos(A + B) = cos A cos B −sin A sin B cos(A −B) = cos A cos B + sin A sin B On subtraction, the cosine products cancel: The difference cos(A + B) −cos(A −B) is −2 sin A sin B, as required: [A1] (b) Start from the first-principles definition and apply the identity from (a): dy f(x + h) −f(x)  dx = f′(x) = lim h h→0 cos(x + h) −cos x  f′(x) = lim h h→0   x+h+x   x+h−x   −2 sin sin f′(x) = lim 2 2  h→0 h      −2 sin 2x+h sin h  2 2 f′(x) = lim h  h→0\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-k/q5-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"For small h in radians, sin(h/2) ∼h/2; equivalently sin(h/2)/(h/2) →1. With P = x + h, Q = x, the difference quotient is cos(x + h) −cos x = −sin(x + h/2)sin(h/2) . [B1] [A1] h h/2 As h →0, the last factor tends to 1 and the sine factor tends to sin x. [M1] [A1] Thus the derivative is −sin x . [M1] [A1] Source clarification. The printed prompt labels both parts (a). The second is labelled (b) here:\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 5 is 10 marks.</p>"
    ],
