    "id": "madas/alevel-pure-k/q8",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-k/q8-question-1.svg\" alt=\"Use partial fractions to determine, in exact simplified form, the value of the following integral. 1  2 3 2 2 x − 5 x + 5 dx . ( 10 ) ( 2 )( 2 ) x − 3 x + 2 x − 2 x + 1 0\" style=\"--madas-width:580.0px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-k/q8-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"The denominator factors as (x −2)(x −1)3. [M1] [A1] The two original factors are x2 −3x + 2 = (x −2)(x −1) and x2 −2x + 1 = (x −1)2. Write the source decomposition and clear its denominator: 2x3 −5x2 + 5 A B C D (x −2)(x −1)3 ≡ x −2 + (x −1)3 + (x −1)2 + x −1 2x3 −5x2 + 5 ≡A(x −1)3 + B(x −2) + C(x −1)(x −2) + D(x −2)(x −1)2 Substitute 1 and 2 to isolate two coefficients: x = 1 : 2 = −B, B = −2 x = 2 : 1 = A Substitute 0 and then 3: 5 = −A −2B + 2C −2D 5 = −1 + 4 + 2C −2D 2 = 2C −2D\" style=\"--madas-width:584.0px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-k/q8-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"C −D = 1 14 = 8A + B + 2C + 4D 14 = 8 −2 + 2C + 4D 8 = 2C + 4D C + 2D = 4 Subtract the equations C −D = 1, C + 2D = 4: 3D = 3, D = 1, C = 2. With z = x −1, the numerator is 2z3 + z2 −4z + 2. [M1] [A1] Matching coefficients after multiplying by (z −1)z3 gives the decomposition z −1 + 1 1 z + 2 z2 −2 z3 . [M1] [M1] [A1] In terms of x, integrate the four terms separately: 1 Z 1 1 2 x −2 −2(x −1)−3 + 2(x −1)−2 + . . . = x −1 dx 0 i 1 ln |x −2| + (x −1)−2 −2(x −1)−1 + ln |x −1| h 2 = 0\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-k/q8-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"The upper value is ln(3/2) + ln(1/2) + 4 + 4, the lower value ln 2 + ln 1 + 1 + 2. Subtracting gives 5 + ln[(3/2)(1/2)/2] = 5 + ln(3/8). The integral is therefore 1/2  2 1 ln |(x −2)(x −1)| − x −1 + = 5 + ln(3/8) . [M1] [M1] [A1] (x −1)2 0\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
