    "id": "madas/alevel-pure-k/q9",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-k/q9-question-1.svg\" alt=\"Ladan is repaying an interest free loan of £6200 over a period of n months, in such a way so that her monthly repayments form an arithmetic series. She repays £350 in the first month, £340 in the second month, £330 in the third month and so on until the full loan is repaid. ( ) Determine, showing a full algebraic method, the value of n . 7\" style=\"--madas-width:582.7px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-k/q9-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"The n-th payment is 350 −10(n −1). [B1] [A1] The sequence is 350 + 340 + 330 + · · · = 6200. With a = 350, d = −10, apply the arithmetic sum and simplify: Sn = n 2 [2a + (n −1)d] 6200 = n 2 [2 × 350 + (n −1)(−10)] 6200 = n 2 [700 −10n + 10] 6200 = n 2 [710 −10n] 620 = n 2 (71 −n) 1240 = n(71 −n) 1240 = 71n −n2\" style=\"--madas-width:449.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-k/q9-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"n2 −71n + 1240 = 0 The arithmetic sum satisfies n2 −71n + 1240 = (n −31)(n −40) = 0. 6200 = n 2 [700 −10(n −1)], [M1] [A1] The quadratic formula also gives q 712 −4(1240))/2 n = (71 ± . = (71 ± 9)/2 Check the final payment in each case: u31 = 350 + 30(−10) = 50, whereas u40 = 350 + 39(−10) . = −40 The 40-month root would require a nonpositive monthly payment at the end and is infeasible: [A1] Hence n = 31 . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 9 is 7 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "Ladan is repaying an interest free loan of £6200 over a period of n months, in such a way so that her monthly repayments form an arithmetic series. She repays £350 in the first month, £340 in the second month, £330 in the third month and so on until the full loan is repaid. ( ) Determine, showing a full algebraic method, the value of n . 7"
